1
00:01:40,159 --> 00:01:45,500
Grandpa! I got thirty red circles! I got a whole thirty circles!

2
00:01:46,199 --> 00:01:51,556
Oh? Let me see. Hmm, thirty circles, huh?

3
00:01:53,029 --> 00:01:54,460
You did great!

4
00:01:55,129 --> 00:01:56,340
I did it!

5
00:02:00,509 --> 00:02:02,880
Mokku, you've really become a good boy.

6
00:02:04,359 --> 00:02:09,118
It's true! I became a good boy. Next, I'm going to be an honor student!

7
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:24,280
Are you that happy?

8
00:02:24,575 --> 00:02:28,663
The teacher told us that having good grades isn't enough to make you an honor student.

9
00:02:29,269 --> 00:02:32,475
You also have to help out properly at home.

10
00:02:34,470 --> 00:02:36,187
Huh? You don't get it, Grandpa.

11
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:37,320
Huh?

12
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:41,680
Well, Mokku has really changed. Good for him.

13
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:44,940
W-What the...!

14
00:02:47,170 --> 00:02:49,120
Mokku, wh-what are you doing?!

15
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:53,049
I learned in school that mice are filthy animals!

16
00:02:53,458 --> 00:02:54,698
What did you say?!

17
00:02:55,610 --> 00:03:02,159
Mice are bad animals that ravage crops and food, and even carry infectious germs!

18
00:03:02,765 --> 00:03:05,412
How dare you say that! That's sewer rats!

19
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:07,360
I'm a respectable field mouse!

20
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,316
Stop it, stop it, stop it! Cut it out!

21
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:12,252
But Redbeard, you've never washed your hands or face, have you?

22
00:03:12,509 --> 00:03:14,127
You really are filthy.

23
00:03:15,724 --> 00:03:17,799
Damn you! Take this!

24
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:27,638
Did you forget that I'm an oak puppet, Redbeard?

25
00:03:31,675 --> 00:03:33,930
What, you got picked on?

26
00:03:34,087 --> 00:03:35,400
Yes, exactly.

27
00:03:38,410 --> 00:03:39,720
Well, take a seat.

28
00:03:40,348 --> 00:03:41,175
Yes.

29
00:03:42,090 --> 00:03:48,986
This isn't just about me. It concerns you too, Big Bro Kenken, and Hanaguro.
Concerns us, too?

30
00:03:49,239 --> 00:03:56,980
Yes. That Mokku has the nerve to say animals are filthy. And he told me to go live with Big Bro Kenken...

31
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:01,440
This is a matter of honor for all animals.

32
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:08,980
Exactly! Just because Mokku's been acting like a good boy lately, he's looking down on us animals.

33
00:04:09,214 --> 00:04:11,100
- It makes me sick! 
- Unforgivable!

34
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:19,040
Right? Even today, just because he got a perfect score in art class for the first time, he's getting cocky and saying he'll become an honor student.

35
00:04:19,905 --> 00:04:21,500
Now that pisses me off even more.

36
00:04:21,655 --> 00:04:25,060
You've got to take a stand here, Big Bro Kenken.

37
00:04:25,525 --> 00:04:29,914
All right! Animals of the world, rise up!

38
00:04:30,063 --> 00:04:31,640
Yeah!

39
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:49,902
That's the third time!

40
00:04:50,105 --> 00:04:52,016
Damn fish!

41
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:53,560
All right, this time for sure!

42
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:01,900
Oh, hello there, Mokku.

43
00:05:02,225 --> 00:05:03,120
What do you want?

44
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,840
Oh, nothing. You were fishing here yesterday, too, weren't you?

45
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,040
Yeah.

46
00:05:07,930 --> 00:05:08,930
How are they biting today?

47
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:13,020
Not a thing. You were here the day before yesterday, too, right? How was it then?

48
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:14,900
No luck at all.

49
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:17,040
Oh, really?

50
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:22,900
Huh, not a single one? But why come out here every day?

51
00:05:23,470 --> 00:05:25,700
Because I'm a good boy now!

52
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:28,600
That's right. Good for you, Mokku. Keep it up.

53
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:30,320
Mokku, what's wrong?

54
00:05:31,105 --> 00:05:32,480
It's nothing.

55
00:05:33,585 --> 00:05:36,820
I wanted to catch lots of fish for Grandpa to eat, but...

56
00:05:37,155 --> 00:05:39,580
...I'm not very good at fishing.

57
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:42,680
Is that so? That makes me happy.

58
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:47,260
I had no idea my pal Mokku was so attached to his Grandpa.

59
00:05:48,450 --> 00:05:51,020
Hey, please. Let me help you out.

60
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:51,520
Huh?

61
00:05:51,805 --> 00:05:55,120
I've got it! I know a place packed with fish.

62
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:57,200
You're not bad at fishing, Mokku.

63
00:05:57,375 --> 00:06:04,240
You just don't know where they are. / But Kenken, we were never really friends...

64
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:16,620
That's because I didn't know what a kind kid you were! Forgive me for before. From today on, I'm your best friend! / Do you really know a place with lots of fish?

65
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:22,900
Of course I do! Let me show you the way. I was truly touched by your kind heart, Mokku.

66
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:24,720
All right, I'm counting on you.

67
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:27,900
Good, good. Come on, let's go, let's go, let's go.

68
00:06:29,730 --> 00:06:32,620
You can't go, Mokku. You mustn't go!

69
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:39,240
Aren't I your best friend? If something terrible happens to you, don't come crying to me.

70
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:54,460
Heave-ho!

71
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:55,520
Not yet?

72
00:06:55,970 --> 00:06:57,820
Not yet. I wonder why.

73
00:06:58,770 --> 00:07:02,680
Caught him fast, didn't you? No need to rush like that, though.

74
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:13,100
Tied up tight.

75
00:07:18,010 --> 00:07:23,700
Still, Mokku's a good kid, catching fish for his grandfather.

76
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:27,160
I'll get along with all of you, too.

77
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:30,340
And I'm going to be a model student, too!

78
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:34,120
Now, catch a whole bunch right here.

79
00:07:34,485 --> 00:07:36,980
The bottom of the lake is full of fish.

80
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:48,720
Today, I'm going to give Grandfather plenty of fish to eat!

81
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:56,400
Oh no! The boat is sinking!

82
00:07:58,710 --> 00:08:00,420
Mokku! Jump!

83
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:01,760
Big brother!

84
00:08:02,179 --> 00:08:03,179
We did it!

85
00:08:18,415 --> 00:08:21,820
Mine! Mine! Mine!

86
00:08:28,550 --> 00:08:29,550
Boss!

87
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:33,419
It went well, didn't it? Damn right it did.

88
00:08:39,569 --> 00:08:43,000
Heh, now the old man is yours forever.

89
00:08:43,465 --> 00:08:47,020
That's what happens when a mere puppet tries to become a model student.

90
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,040
Yeah, he's furious.

91
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:55,000
I'll have them bring over all my favorite foods, lots of delicious things. I wonder why.

92
00:08:55,149 --> 00:09:02,160
I understand completely. Well then, I'll be going... Excuse me!

93
00:09:04,795 --> 00:09:08,800
Now we can milk him for all he's worth. I'm so happy.

94
00:09:09,185 --> 00:09:11,940
Forget that, let's wait and see a little longer.

95
00:09:12,445 --> 00:09:15,240
He's got the devil's own luck, after all.

96
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:22,640
That's the great thing about you, Brother. Always so cautious. I wonder why, though?

97
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:23,860
Heh-heh.

98
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:56,140
Is Mokku done for at last? Guess he couldn't float back up after all.

99
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:26,180
(water splashing)

100
00:10:26,181 --> 00:10:27,480
Goodbye, Mokku...

101
00:10:32,039 --> 00:10:33,060
Mokku!

102
00:10:33,530 --> 00:10:34,530
Cricket!

103
00:10:37,909 --> 00:10:41,000
Mokku, thank goodness! I'm so glad!

104
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:44,600
My leg... I left one of my legs at the bottom of the lake.

105
00:10:45,385 --> 00:10:46,385
Your leg?

106
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:48,320
Yeah. I'm going to get it back.

107
00:10:49,229 --> 00:10:51,020
Ah, wait, wait!

108
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,760
Oh, Mokku, you idiot!

109
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:58,500
You just barely survived! Throwing your life away over a leg is completely pointless!

110
00:10:58,870 --> 00:11:00,700
Idiot! Idiot! Big idiot!

111
00:11:27,199 --> 00:11:28,460
Look, he's back!

112
00:11:28,984 --> 00:11:30,040
He's standing up!

113
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:32,120
Oh no, run!

114
00:11:32,305 --> 00:11:33,780
Yeah, that's it! Run, run!

115
00:11:45,749 --> 00:11:47,320
Mokku! What happened?!

116
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:48,020
Huh?

117
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:49,120
Mokku!

118
00:11:50,759 --> 00:11:51,759
Grandpa!

119
00:11:56,969 --> 00:12:00,060
Mokku! Stay right there! Stay right where you are!

120
00:12:07,589 --> 00:12:10,480
Mokku! What on earth happened?!

121
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:12,140
Grandpa!

122
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:16,380
There, there. It's all right now, it's all right.

123
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:17,485
Grandpa!

124
00:12:34,219 --> 00:12:35,600
Grandpa, I'm heading out!

125
00:12:35,915 --> 00:12:40,220
Right, be careful on your way. How is your leg holding up, eh?

126
00:12:40,910 --> 00:12:44,020
Much better than before! Look, see?

127
00:12:46,109 --> 00:12:49,080
Hey, stop that! You'll break it again if you're so reckless!

128
00:12:49,849 --> 00:12:53,120
I'll be fine! Grandpa's the best in the world!

129
00:12:56,239 --> 00:12:57,460
Mokku!

130
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:01,940
Huh?

131
00:13:04,449 --> 00:13:07,800
Grandpa, help! I can't walk like this!

132
00:13:07,975 --> 00:13:10,780
I told you not to be so reckless!

133
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:12,580
Hold still...

134
00:13:19,899 --> 00:13:24,300
There, that should do it. Don't go hanging around with Kenken and Hanaguro anymore, you hear?

135
00:13:24,749 --> 00:13:28,180
I know. I'm off!

136
00:13:30,359 --> 00:13:32,340
Study hard, now!

137
00:13:33,769 --> 00:13:34,860
See ya!

138
00:13:46,745 --> 00:13:49,880
Well, well, Mokku. Aren't you devout?

139
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:53,920
Oh, it's just you, Nora. I have to get to school. See ya.

140
00:13:55,580 --> 00:14:01,520
Wait, wait, Mokku. You have a chance to become a real human, and you're just throwing it away? Foolish Mokku.

141
00:14:01,725 --> 00:14:04,160
Liar! You've got to be lying!

142
00:14:04,345 --> 00:14:07,560
God would punish me if I told a lie in front of a church.

143
00:14:07,855 --> 00:14:09,140
I'm still going to school.

144
00:14:10,924 --> 00:14:16,200
Hey, Mokku. If you want to become a real human, you should enter a monastery.

145
00:14:17,859 --> 00:14:19,460
Just like a priest.

146
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:21,260
A priest?

147
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:26,080
That's right. Even priests have to enter a monastery to become one.

148
00:14:31,259 --> 00:14:35,260
If you train at a monastery too, Mokku, you'll surely become a real human.

149
00:14:36,739 --> 00:14:41,220
If you head south past two mountains from here, there's a Camaldolese monastery.

150
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:43,980
I hear the abbot is a very kind man.

151
00:14:56,279 --> 00:14:58,720
Thank you, Nora. I'll go check it out!

152
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:07,360
(Laughs)

153
00:15:07,599 --> 00:15:12,420
Heh heh heh. You're so good at this. A true genius. I wonder why?

154
00:15:12,590 --> 00:15:17,240
The honor of all animals is riding on this plan. Thank you, Nora.

155
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:24,340
I don't care about thanks. Deceiving people is just my hobby. You better hurry or you won't make it in time.

156
00:15:24,885 --> 00:15:27,460
Oh, right! Off to Hanakuro!

157
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:32,060
Roger that! We can't fail this time. I wonder why?

158
00:15:32,359 --> 00:15:38,460
Brother, big brother, slacker, slacker, slacker, slacker!

159
00:15:59,179 --> 00:16:00,980
Welcome, Mokku.

160
00:16:02,739 --> 00:16:05,260
Why? How do you know my name?

161
00:16:06,139 --> 00:16:09,960
God sees all. Even your wish.

162
00:16:10,195 --> 00:16:12,140
However, the training will be severe.

163
00:16:12,365 --> 00:16:16,180
If it means becoming a real human, I'll endure any hardship.

164
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:21,560
That's a good attitude. God will surely grant you a miracle.

165
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:52,660
This is severe ascetic penance. If you obey God without food or water for three days, your wish will be granted in an instant.

166
00:16:53,275 --> 00:16:56,320
I'm a wooden puppet, so going without food is no problem for me.

167
00:16:56,575 --> 00:16:57,820
Oh, good boy.

168
00:17:02,999 --> 00:17:05,160
It feels like becoming divine, doesn't it?

169
00:17:05,559 --> 00:17:09,060
Indeed. Blessed are those who believe.

170
00:17:12,129 --> 00:17:14,720
I'll be back in three days without fail.

171
00:17:15,074 --> 00:17:16,780
Yes, I'll be fine.

172
00:17:17,469 --> 00:17:21,200
Ah, now I can finally become a real human.

173
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:34,480
Heh heh...

174
00:17:40,060 --> 00:17:49,280
That Mokku will dry up and die, completely unaware it's the end of the line for him, yet he still thinks he can become human. What a fool.

175
00:17:53,429 --> 00:17:56,780
No matter how hard it gets, I will endure it.

176
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:01,360
(gulping sound)

177
00:18:01,361 --> 00:18:02,361
(sobbing)

178
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:08,620
(gulping sound)

179
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:10,620
(sobbing)

180
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:11,600
(gulping sound)

181
00:18:11,601 --> 00:18:11,620
(sobbing)

182
00:18:12,019 --> 00:18:20,640
Water... water... I need water... I'm a wooden puppet, I can't survive without it... Water, water... (sobbing)

183
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:23,580
Mokku, there's nothing I can do!

184
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:23,900
(sobbing)

185
00:18:23,901 --> 00:18:25,920
Water, water...

186
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:27,680
(exhales)

187
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:34,060
(exhales)

188
00:18:34,339 --> 00:18:36,020
Hang in there!

189
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:42,580
(exhales)

190
00:18:45,639 --> 00:18:48,860
Oak Tree Fairy, please help me!

191
00:18:49,094 --> 00:18:50,094
Water...

192
00:18:51,239 --> 00:18:53,760
I do not have that power right now.

193
00:18:54,709 --> 00:19:00,840
But if this keeps up, I'm going to die! I don't want to die! Please, no!

194
00:19:02,420 --> 00:19:10,420
Becoming a real human is not something you achieve by clinging to God or relying on others. You must carve out your own path with your own strength.

195
00:19:10,739 --> 00:19:15,860
I don't want a lecture! Hurry and bring me water! Water!

196
00:19:16,619 --> 00:19:21,820
You have placed yourself in God's hands. All you can do now is await His will.

197
00:19:23,704 --> 00:19:24,960
Ah, wait!

198
00:19:25,919 --> 00:19:29,460
You must reap what you sow.

199
00:19:42,139 --> 00:19:43,760
I don't want to die...

200
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:03,020
Good night. Rain! It's raining!

201
00:20:16,309 --> 00:20:19,120
Just how damn lucky can this brat get?

202
00:20:20,619 --> 00:20:24,160
He was supposed to be completely dried up and dead by now.

203
00:20:26,239 --> 00:20:31,260
Watching him suffer slowly just makes it more fun for us anyway.

204
00:20:31,764 --> 00:20:33,120
And why is that?

205
00:20:35,069 --> 00:20:37,140
Because he's not getting away from us either way, yes.

206
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:38,580
That's right.

207
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:53,800
Ah, help!

208
00:20:58,270 --> 00:20:59,270
Help me!

209
00:21:00,589 --> 00:21:04,160
That guy isn't just going to dry out in the sun—he's going to starve to death!

210
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:05,020
I wonder why?

211
00:21:05,130 --> 00:21:06,020
Shut up!

212
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:08,460
Hehehe, serves him right!

213
00:21:13,729 --> 00:21:15,260
Don't worry! Let's get out of here!

214
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:16,440
Okay!

215
00:21:26,189 --> 00:21:27,189
(Grandpa's voice)

216
00:21:28,900 --> 00:21:29,900
(Grandpa's voice)

217
00:21:33,519 --> 00:21:34,680
Grandpa!

218
00:21:38,049 --> 00:21:39,049
(Grandpa's voice)

219
00:21:39,374 --> 00:21:42,400
You do care about me! You came to save me, didn't you?!

220
00:21:42,780 --> 00:21:43,780
(Grandpa's voice)

221
00:21:45,774 --> 00:21:48,840
Hurry and cut this rope with those proud fangs of yours!

222
00:22:14,089 --> 00:22:16,500
All right, Redbeard, this way next.

223
00:22:17,225 --> 00:22:20,420
Why does it have to be so strange?

224
00:22:29,609 --> 00:22:31,620
All right, Redbeard, climb onto my head.

225
00:22:32,204 --> 00:22:34,280
Hold on tight so you don't fall off.

226
00:22:34,884 --> 00:22:35,900
Take that! Take that!

227
00:22:47,280 --> 00:22:52,140
(Redbeard squeaks)

228
00:22:57,409 --> 00:23:00,360
I'm sorry. You're a fine mouse, Redbeard.

229
00:23:03,869 --> 00:23:05,200
Here you go, Redbeard!

230
00:23:05,959 --> 00:23:07,980
You saved my life.

231
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:13,140
(Laughs)

232
00:23:17,249 --> 00:23:19,880
It's not like I wanted to save you.

233
00:23:22,749 --> 00:23:25,600
From now on, I'm going to get along with humans.

234
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,440
Yeah.

235
00:23:33,309 --> 00:23:40,080
Mokku went to town with Grandfather, but even there, everyone made fun of him, calling him a puppet, and he couldn't help feeling deeply sad.

236
00:23:47,320 --> 00:23:55,320
However, Mereli, the only daughter of a wealthy family, makes the dressed-up Mokku her playmate, unaware that he is a puppet. Mokku soon falls in love with Mereli, and desperate not to be hated, hides the fact that he is a wooden puppet...

237
00:23:55,321 --> 00:24:00,640
...and he could no longer confide the truth. Look forward to next week's Kashi no Ki Mokku!

